WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.430 --> 00:00:03.640
- [Interviewer] All right, Crystal.

00:00:03.640 --> 00:00:04.473
- Yes.

00:00:04.473 --> 00:00:05.306
- [Interviewer] Crystal,
where did you grow up,

00:00:05.306 --> 00:00:06.316
where are you from originally?

00:00:06.316 --> 00:00:09.072
- I was born in Ohio, raised in Virginia

00:00:09.072 --> 00:00:12.877
and raised back and forth
between Ohio and Virginia,

00:00:12.877 --> 00:00:14.483
for a minute.

00:00:15.808 --> 00:00:17.780
- [Interviewer] You grew
up with both your parents?

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:20.106
- No. I grew up with my mom.

00:00:20.106 --> 00:00:24.100
And then I think I was
about three years old

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:26.793
when my grandma got custody of me.

00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:29.056
No, I was four, that's right.

00:00:29.056 --> 00:00:31.610
I was four years old when
my grandma got custody of me

00:00:31.610 --> 00:00:33.380
for about five years.

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:35.215
- [Interviewer] Why'd you leave your mom

00:00:35.215 --> 00:00:36.843
to go to your grandmother?

00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:41.700
- My mom had abusive boyfriends.

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:43.610
I was one years old when she threw me

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:47.340
out of a second story building
due to our beds on fire,

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:48.940
me and my brother.

00:00:48.940 --> 00:00:49.870
She dropped my brother down,

00:00:49.870 --> 00:00:51.380
my brother was like six years old,

00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:53.807
and she literally tossed me out the window

00:00:53.807 --> 00:00:56.280
due to set our beds on fire.

00:00:57.647 --> 00:00:58.970
- [Interviewer] Who set your bed on fire?

00:00:58.970 --> 00:01:01.963
- My mom's ex-boyfriend, Bob I believe.

00:01:09.093 --> 00:01:11.923
It was just too much,
after Bob it was Mike.

00:01:13.138 --> 00:01:18.110
Mike beat us pretty much for
everything under the sun.

00:01:18.110 --> 00:01:19.364
I remember getting my ass whooped,

00:01:19.364 --> 00:01:22.167
my butt whooped, sorry, for-

00:01:22.167 --> 00:01:23.350
- [Interviewer] You can swear.

00:01:23.350 --> 00:01:25.290
- I didn't touch a bug.

00:01:25.290 --> 00:01:27.550
There was a dead bug on the
floor and I didn't pick it up.

00:01:27.550 --> 00:01:30.330
And I got my ass beat,

00:01:30.330 --> 00:01:31.693
with a power hose, innit.

00:01:33.435 --> 00:01:35.913
I was six years old I think for that.

00:01:40.230 --> 00:01:41.610
I don't know, it was crazy.

00:01:41.610 --> 00:01:43.380
- [Interviewer] So a
lot of physical abuse?

00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:45.813
- Yes. A lot of physical,
a lot of mental too.

00:01:46.841 --> 00:01:51.040
Being called names, told
that you're worthless.

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:54.870
The whole nine and it
just never got any better.

00:01:54.870 --> 00:01:57.321
So we went and moved with my grandma.

00:01:57.321 --> 00:01:59.018
- [Interviewer] No sexual abuse?

00:01:59.018 --> 00:02:01.183
- Not until I lived with my grandma.

00:02:02.380 --> 00:02:04.450
When I moved in with my grandmother,

00:02:04.450 --> 00:02:05.620
I was with my grandfather.

00:02:05.620 --> 00:02:10.272
He molested me pretty much
from about the time I was three

00:02:10.272 --> 00:02:12.383
up to about the time I was seven.

00:02:15.020 --> 00:02:17.500
I guess the sad part
about that is my mom knew,

00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:20.070
my grandmother knew and all my aunts knew,

00:02:20.070 --> 00:02:22.323
because he did it to
them when they grew up.

00:02:24.808 --> 00:02:27.160
I'm the only granddaughter
out of my whole family.

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:30.323
It's just me and all my boy cousins,

00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:34.140
they never experienced that.

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:35.790
My grandfather didn't touch them.

00:02:38.586 --> 00:02:40.326
I remember he would get mad at me too.

00:02:40.326 --> 00:02:43.170
It was crazy, he would get mad

00:02:43.170 --> 00:02:45.414
and I'd go tell everybody in there

00:02:45.414 --> 00:02:47.155
and they wouldn't believe me.

00:02:47.155 --> 00:02:49.970
They already knew that happened though,

00:02:49.970 --> 00:02:53.919
so I just don't understand
why they let me go through it

00:02:53.919 --> 00:02:56.258
the way they did, but-

00:02:56.258 --> 00:02:58.780
- [Interviewer] With
a childhood like that,

00:02:58.780 --> 00:03:01.163
where did that take you as an adult?

00:03:02.454 --> 00:03:04.843
- Wow, that's a good question.

00:03:07.530 --> 00:03:11.373
I actually met the father
of my children at a bar.

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:14.010
We have three boys together.

00:03:14.010 --> 00:03:17.733
My oldest is 16, and my youngest is nine.

00:03:20.960 --> 00:03:25.960
Throughout that
relationship he was abusive.

00:03:27.500 --> 00:03:31.563
He used drugs really bad
and hid them from me.

00:03:33.920 --> 00:03:37.415
I think going through what I
went through in my childhood,

00:03:37.415 --> 00:03:41.190
it reflects on the men that I pick now.

00:03:41.190 --> 00:03:44.040
Because every relationship
I've been in has been abusive.

00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:52.113
That put me in a bad spot.

00:03:53.370 --> 00:03:54.810
I use drugs...

00:03:56.940 --> 00:03:58.943
As a comforting mechanism.

00:04:00.670 --> 00:04:04.000
I can't handle it when I'm not high,

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:07.263
it's overwhelming, I wanna give up.

00:04:09.979 --> 00:04:11.763
- [Interviewer] And what is your drug?

00:04:11.763 --> 00:04:12.596
- Heroine.

00:04:12.596 --> 00:04:13.429
- [Interviewer] Heroine?

00:04:13.429 --> 00:04:17.453
- I use heroine, crystal, smoke pot.

00:04:19.060 --> 00:04:20.574
- [Interviewer] And
where are you living now?

00:04:20.574 --> 00:04:24.000
- I currently live on
the streets here of LA.

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:24.833
- [Interviewer] On Skid Row?

00:04:24.833 --> 00:04:27.870
- Yes. I don't have a spot exactly,

00:04:27.870 --> 00:04:29.800
because all my tents get stolen.

00:04:29.800 --> 00:04:32.003
My tents get stolen like clockwork,

00:04:33.490 --> 00:04:35.240
so I gave up on having a spot,

00:04:35.240 --> 00:04:39.050
I just bounce around from spot to spot.

00:04:39.050 --> 00:04:40.210
Go around to people I know.

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:43.010
- [Interviewer] And how do
you support yourself now?

00:04:43.010 --> 00:04:43.890
- I panhandle.

00:04:43.890 --> 00:04:46.190
I fly a sign on a corner,

00:04:46.190 --> 00:04:47.483
I ask people for money.

00:04:49.090 --> 00:04:51.893
I get rejected a lot, like a lot.

00:04:53.420 --> 00:04:55.483
I'm lucky to make 10, 15 bucks a day.

00:04:57.290 --> 00:04:59.143
But it's life.

00:05:00.280 --> 00:05:01.113
- [Interviewer] You're not doing

00:05:01.113 --> 00:05:02.993
what some of the other
girls will do for money?

00:05:04.810 --> 00:05:05.643
- I have.

00:05:07.680 --> 00:05:08.513
I'm not gonna lie.

00:05:08.513 --> 00:05:10.280
I'm not gonna sit here and lie, I have.

00:05:12.659 --> 00:05:14.913
But that was only when
I was really hard up.

00:05:16.440 --> 00:05:17.590
I'm the type person...

00:05:20.236 --> 00:05:21.373
I treasure myself.

00:05:22.520 --> 00:05:26.770
I did anyways, I'd rather
go out here and work

00:05:26.770 --> 00:05:28.583
my hands dirty and make money,

00:05:30.560 --> 00:05:31.870
instead of sell myself

00:05:31.870 --> 00:05:34.200
because that's just not
in the cards for me,

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:36.054
it don't work for me.

00:05:36.054 --> 00:05:39.060
I've done it once, maybe twice that's it.

00:05:39.060 --> 00:05:42.143
I couldn't do it, I felt degraded.

00:05:43.420 --> 00:05:45.950
- [Interviewer] Yeah, I think
it affects everyone that way.

00:05:45.950 --> 00:05:46.783
- Yeah, so-

00:05:46.783 --> 00:05:47.840
- [Interviewer] Whether
they realize it or not.

00:05:47.840 --> 00:05:51.870
- Yeah, it just is not for me.

00:05:51.870 --> 00:05:55.063
I'll go out here and paint a
house or wash somebody's car,

00:05:55.950 --> 00:05:57.553
mechanically work on something.

00:05:58.580 --> 00:05:59.893
I've got mad talent,

00:06:02.570 --> 00:06:04.073
it just goes to waste.

00:06:05.481 --> 00:06:06.580
- [Interviewer] Do you have kids?

00:06:06.580 --> 00:06:08.200
- I do, I have four.

00:06:08.200 --> 00:06:09.439
Three boys and a girl.

00:06:09.439 --> 00:06:10.642
- [Interviewer] And where are they?

00:06:10.642 --> 00:06:12.420
- My three boys are currently

00:06:12.420 --> 00:06:14.803
with my ex mother in law down in Florida.

00:06:18.780 --> 00:06:20.930
They're pretty much
the only family I have.

00:06:22.610 --> 00:06:25.053
My entire family passed
away last December.

00:06:29.140 --> 00:06:31.870
December 11th is my mother's birthday,

00:06:31.870 --> 00:06:33.540
the father of my children...

00:06:38.760 --> 00:06:41.610
My mom passed away
December ninth last year,

00:06:41.610 --> 00:06:45.010
and the father of my children
passed away December 11th.

00:06:45.010 --> 00:06:47.753
Then my brother killed
himself on December 12th,

00:06:48.819 --> 00:06:51.180
and then my dad down here,
my biological father,

00:06:51.180 --> 00:06:52.603
he died December 17th.

00:06:57.670 --> 00:06:59.893
And then my best friend,

00:07:01.415 --> 00:07:03.210
I was in a relationship with him

00:07:03.210 --> 00:07:04.261
after the father of my children,

00:07:04.261 --> 00:07:08.000
he passed away on December
20th, all last year.

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:08.883
- [Interviewer] Wow.

00:07:11.706 --> 00:07:14.883
- I hate to say it, but I
really haven't mourned that.

00:07:16.580 --> 00:07:18.770
I haven't mourned any of them yet.

00:07:18.770 --> 00:07:20.120
I've just kept myself high.

00:07:22.999 --> 00:07:26.493
My daughter's three, she's down here.

00:07:27.920 --> 00:07:30.298
She's actually about
four blocks from here.

00:07:30.298 --> 00:07:32.090
- [Interviewer] Who is she staying with?

00:07:32.090 --> 00:07:34.043
- She stays with this older couple.

00:07:34.043 --> 00:07:36.510
I met the lady online

00:07:36.510 --> 00:07:39.150
through a pen pal thing through my email.

00:07:39.150 --> 00:07:42.890
And I've been talking to her
for probably about six years.

00:07:42.890 --> 00:07:44.770
And she told me her life story,

00:07:44.770 --> 00:07:47.280
she was in a car accident,
couldn't have kids.

00:07:47.280 --> 00:07:49.363
And her husband was looking to adopt.

00:07:50.690 --> 00:07:52.100
I found out I was pregnant,

00:07:52.100 --> 00:07:53.460
and as soon as I found out I told her.

00:07:53.460 --> 00:07:56.927
Because I'm living on
the street, I use drugs.

00:07:56.927 --> 00:07:58.343
I can't have a kid out here.

00:07:59.300 --> 00:08:00.440
And I told her about it

00:08:00.440 --> 00:08:03.563
and I got myself clean for that year.

00:08:04.570 --> 00:08:08.440
I maintained the pregnancy
and she came out beautiful.

00:08:08.440 --> 00:08:13.250
She's healthy, she's
an amazing little girl.

00:08:13.250 --> 00:08:18.113
And I signed her over to
them immediately at birth.

00:08:19.470 --> 00:08:21.530
And I think that was
probably the best thing

00:08:21.530 --> 00:08:22.833
I could do for her.

00:08:26.120 --> 00:08:27.593
She's a little angel.

00:08:30.036 --> 00:08:31.460
She's beautiful.

00:08:31.460 --> 00:08:34.840
She's like somebody plucked
her off a store shelf.

00:08:34.840 --> 00:08:36.643
She's just fucking beautiful.

00:08:37.490 --> 00:08:39.670
And she's amazingly happy right there,

00:08:39.670 --> 00:08:43.133
I could not have made a better
choice for her as a parent.

00:08:45.410 --> 00:08:46.860
People might call me a shitty parent

00:08:46.860 --> 00:08:48.273
for that but I don't.

00:08:49.130 --> 00:08:51.130
If I was a shitty parent
I would've done drugs

00:08:51.130 --> 00:08:53.920
and kept the baby living on the streets,

00:08:53.920 --> 00:08:55.070
that's a shitty parent.

00:08:56.070 --> 00:08:57.323
Giving her a life though,

00:08:58.429 --> 00:09:00.343
that's a good parent to me.

00:09:02.160 --> 00:09:04.420
- [Interviewer] What's the
hardest part of your life?

00:09:04.420 --> 00:09:05.390
- Being away from my kids-

00:09:05.390 --> 00:09:06.840
- [Interviewer] Yeah.

00:09:06.840 --> 00:09:07.673
- My three children,

00:09:07.673 --> 00:09:09.240
I was with them from
the time they were born.

00:09:09.240 --> 00:09:10.960
I was a stay-at-home mom,

00:09:10.960 --> 00:09:12.563
I loved being a mom, bro.

00:09:13.820 --> 00:09:15.413
My kids are everything to me.

00:09:18.400 --> 00:09:21.088
And it sucks I have no
contact with them now,

00:09:21.088 --> 00:09:23.563
because of my drug use.

00:09:27.588 --> 00:09:28.720
And that hurts.

00:09:28.720 --> 00:09:31.703
That is definitely the
hardest part of my life.

00:09:33.520 --> 00:09:34.770
Because I've been out here six years,

00:09:34.770 --> 00:09:35.920
almost seven years now.

00:09:38.880 --> 00:09:39.713
I'm stuck.

00:09:40.980 --> 00:09:42.880
- [Interviewer] Do you see any
hope of getting out of here,

00:09:42.880 --> 00:09:44.310
getting clean?

00:09:44.310 --> 00:09:45.143
- I hope so.

00:09:47.150 --> 00:09:50.710
As of right now, I can honestly say no.

00:09:50.710 --> 00:09:52.333
I can't see that in my future.

00:09:54.180 --> 00:09:59.180
Only because, like I said, I'm stuck.

00:09:59.250 --> 00:10:00.777
I'm a heroine addict.

00:10:05.684 --> 00:10:08.513
Until that drug stops, I can't go home.

00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:14.010
They're being well taken care of,

00:10:14.010 --> 00:10:16.423
I'm very grateful to my mother in law.

00:10:18.800 --> 00:10:21.763
That woman has earned
so much of my respect.

00:10:22.630 --> 00:10:25.090
She's number one in my books, bro.

00:10:25.090 --> 00:10:27.050
Hands down, she's amazing.

00:10:27.050 --> 00:10:28.800
She's raising three of my children,

00:10:30.060 --> 00:10:31.983
she's doing something that I couldn't do.

00:10:33.441 --> 00:10:35.441
And I'm highly grateful to her for that.

00:10:37.110 --> 00:10:39.070
- [Interviewer] You went
through a lot as a child.

00:10:39.070 --> 00:10:41.930
Is there something that
you would pin point

00:10:41.930 --> 00:10:44.570
as the main reason that you're
in this predicament today,

00:10:44.570 --> 00:10:46.120
that happened back then?

00:10:46.120 --> 00:10:46.953
- My mother.

00:10:49.610 --> 00:10:52.223
That's baseline, my mom
was a shitty parent.

00:10:54.490 --> 00:10:56.540
She chose men and the bars

00:10:56.540 --> 00:10:58.190
more than she chose me and my brother.

00:10:58.190 --> 00:10:59.840
My brother practically raised me.

00:11:01.120 --> 00:11:02.320
My brother is the one who told me

00:11:02.320 --> 00:11:04.330
about woman having a period.

00:11:04.330 --> 00:11:07.950
He's the one who taught
me how to use Kotex.

00:11:07.950 --> 00:11:11.310
That's crazy, I blame my mother.

00:11:11.310 --> 00:11:14.293
My mom is the reason that
my kids were taken from me.

00:11:15.340 --> 00:11:16.660
All because I did not order her food

00:11:16.660 --> 00:11:18.373
correctly over the phone.

00:11:19.631 --> 00:11:23.800
She called Children Services
and she trashed my house

00:11:23.800 --> 00:11:26.440
and told them that I smoke
pot and they drug tested me,

00:11:26.440 --> 00:11:29.490
and seen my house all dirty
and they took my kids.

00:11:29.490 --> 00:11:30.710
Because of her.

00:11:30.710 --> 00:11:33.653
I blame my mom for every
situation I'm in right now.

00:11:35.060 --> 00:11:36.810
I know that's not cool to say,

00:11:36.810 --> 00:11:38.050
but that's the truth.

00:11:38.050 --> 00:11:40.100
I'm not gonna sit here and lie to nobody.

00:11:41.790 --> 00:11:45.353
My mom is definitely the
baseline of my problems.

00:11:48.610 --> 00:11:53.610
Definitely, but it hasn't been
easy for me out here either.

00:11:54.150 --> 00:11:59.150
Its just as hard, I have to
fight for everything I have.

00:11:59.590 --> 00:12:01.610
My shit get stolen all the time.

00:12:01.610 --> 00:12:03.460
I've been raped three times out here.

00:12:05.360 --> 00:12:06.403
I've been beat up.

00:12:08.310 --> 00:12:10.641
You name it, it's happened to me.

00:12:10.641 --> 00:12:12.600
- [Interviewer] It's a rough neighborhood.

00:12:12.600 --> 00:12:14.550
- But hey, I'm still alive and kicking.

00:12:15.710 --> 00:12:17.783
The worse thing I got is a scar.

00:12:19.345 --> 00:12:20.550
It's not safe being a single,

00:12:20.550 --> 00:12:23.940
white bitch out here in
California on the streets.

00:12:23.940 --> 00:12:27.063
I make it happen though, no matter what.

00:12:27.063 --> 00:12:30.490
- [Interviewer] What do you worry about?

00:12:30.490 --> 00:12:32.490
- What do I worry about,
out here on the streets-

00:12:32.490 --> 00:12:34.390
- [Interviewer] What's
your biggest concern.

00:12:34.390 --> 00:12:37.440
- My biggest concern in life period,

00:12:37.440 --> 00:12:39.100
is not making it home to my kids,

00:12:39.100 --> 00:12:41.250
or making it home and them rejecting me

00:12:41.250 --> 00:12:43.600
for me being gone for so long.

00:12:43.600 --> 00:12:45.620
I'm terrified of that.

00:12:45.620 --> 00:12:46.954
- [Interviewer] Is shame a big part of-

00:12:46.954 --> 00:12:51.463
- Extremely. I'm ashamed,
I'm disappointed.

00:12:57.390 --> 00:13:02.323
It's almost like a disgrace
to my relatives to my family,

00:13:03.493 --> 00:13:05.253
for me to be out here.

00:13:08.100 --> 00:13:10.293
I'm very ashamed to be out here.

00:13:12.384 --> 00:13:14.880
I'm a certified genius, bro.

00:13:14.880 --> 00:13:16.083
I have a certificate.

00:13:17.170 --> 00:13:20.020
I was in the Air Force.

00:13:20.020 --> 00:13:22.050
I went to nursing school, I'm an RN.

00:13:22.050 --> 00:13:23.603
I'm a certified RN,

00:13:25.966 --> 00:13:28.166
but I'm out here on the
streets doing drugs.

00:13:31.416 --> 00:13:34.560
It's a fucked up thing.

00:13:34.560 --> 00:13:35.520
- [Interviewer] What's
the most important lesson

00:13:35.520 --> 00:13:37.480
that you've learnt in your life?

00:13:44.621 --> 00:13:48.582
- The most important
lesson I've learnt now is

00:13:48.582 --> 00:13:52.313
if you have good parents
or people who raised you,

00:13:55.620 --> 00:13:57.862
respect them though.

00:13:57.862 --> 00:14:00.540
Have that respect for your elders,

00:14:00.540 --> 00:14:02.540
give them the appreciation
that they deserve,

00:14:02.540 --> 00:14:05.763
because not many people get that in life.

00:14:09.690 --> 00:14:12.090
A hard lesson I've learnt
is don't judge people.

00:14:13.060 --> 00:14:14.570
You don't know anybody's story,

00:14:14.570 --> 00:14:15.853
everybody has one.

00:14:16.970 --> 00:14:18.343
Everybody has a story.

00:14:19.490 --> 00:14:21.403
Don't judge anybody by a cover.

00:14:23.360 --> 00:14:25.693
Because you don't know what
they went through in their life.

00:14:28.760 --> 00:14:29.593
- [Interviewer] All right, Crystal.

00:14:29.593 --> 00:14:31.070
Thank you so much for sharing your story.

00:14:31.070 --> 00:14:31.920
